Description: BLE-MIDI capability for pi-Stomp
 Ships a bluetooth.service drop-in that starts bluetoothd with -E, which is
 what registers bluez's BLE-MIDI GATT profile, and unblocks the rfkill soft
 block the Pi 5 radio boots with. Once a BLE-MIDI device connects, bluez
 publishes an ALSA seq port and jackd -X seq bridges it automatically.
 .
 Installing this package does not turn Bluetooth on; the drop-in is inert
 while bluetooth.service is disabled. The pi-Stomp UI owns enable/disable
 and all pairing.

